WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
I also like the example you have in the

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.880
book with the uh monkey on the back. You

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:10.520
know, that basically if you if you guide

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.400
your staff through the like not leaving

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.120
the monkey on your desk and taking the

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.000
monkey back out the room again so they

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.400
can solve their own issues.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.480
Uh I thought that was a great analogy to

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.840
kind of

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.240
bring back the point that if you solve

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.760
all these problems on the business owner

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.160
level, you will never build a big

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.080
business.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.520
>> I think one of the keys to delegation

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.400
and there's two levels to delegation, by

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.000
the way. There's delegating tasks, which

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.120
are repeatable, they're done on a

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.880
framework. Um there's delegating tasks

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.400
and then there's delegating

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.640
um decisions.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.240
So,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.440
you can get a you can build a really big

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.560
business and you can get really wealthy

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.960
by delegating only tasks.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.200
Meaning, nobody in your business makes

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.880
decisions except for you.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.600
And this is the business owner where the

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.600
phone rings all day.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.000
All the employees are calling him all

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.960
the time wanting to know what to do in

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.559
certain situations. He can't go on

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.160
vacation. He works all the time. But,

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.480
you can build you can build wealth that

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.920
way. You can you can get wealthy.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.080
When it comes to time to delegate

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.280
decisions, which is the second level,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.520
my favorite thing to do is

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.320
when an employee comes to me with a

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.880
problem, that problem is

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.440
like you think of it as a monkey on the

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.360
employee's back.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.480
They come into my office and they tell

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.280
me their problem. As soon as they tell

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.040
me their problem, the monkey jumps off

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.440
of their back and it jumps onto my back.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.840
Now I have a monkey on my back and their

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.480
problem and I have two options. I can

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.600
say, all right, get out of my office,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.120
I'll solve it.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.840
I'll take you I'll take your monkey or

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.520
to try to find a way to send them out

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.320
with their monkey and their problem and

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.440
a way to solution and and a and a way to

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.000
solve it.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.320
The easy way is to say, get out of my

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.520
office, I'll take care of this.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.440
But, then at 5:00 you have an office

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.280
full of monkeys.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.800
Um [laughter]

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.800
so, yeah, it's a it's a harder in the

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.160
near term but better in the long-term to

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.600
ask the right questions, ask the right

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.160
follow-up. And an example of this is

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.720
back in the days and still running

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.080
storage running a storage facility, one

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.039
of my reps would answer her phone and

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.039
and then they'd call me. They'd say,

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:11.880
"Nick,

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:16.080
you know, somebody just called and they

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:18.120
rented unit 69 70. They rented unit 70.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.480
What? 70's got a lock on it.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.440
What do I do?

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.760
Somebody else has already rented it."

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:24.520
I'm like, "Okay. The answer to this for

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.800
me is very simple.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.280
Try to find a different unit available,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.440
but I'm going to ask a question back to

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.720
them. Okay, what's our goal?

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.760
What's our goal?"

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.280
And they'll say, "Oh, our goal is to

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.680
rent storage units."

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.800
"Okay, if our goal is to rent storage

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.040
units, that unit's not empty, what do

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.280
you think is a reasonable solution here

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.720
to this problem?"

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.000
They'll say, "Oh, well,

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.120
I don't know." And if they say I don't

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.120
know, you just kind of realize that they

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.720
don't have what it takes to start to

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.200
make decisions and they're incompetent

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.280
and they're they've reached the level of

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.959
their competence, but many of them will

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.760
get it and they'll say, "Oh, you know,

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:55.480
the the the facility's only 75%

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.640
occupied. We have 25% units still

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.880
available. Right next to unit 70 is unit

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.160
69. It's open. There's I can tell the

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.160
customer to go in that one. I'll change

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.680
over the rental and then we're

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.400
the problem is solved."

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.160
I'll say, "Okay, great. Get out of my

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.640
office. Take your monkey with you."

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.880
So, it's uh when you do that over and

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.480
over again,

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:15.239
two things happen.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.160
Number one, you get a look into the mind

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:18.959
of your employee.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.760
You start to see how they think about

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:22.080
things and you can judge their level of

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.640
competence.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.280
Can I start to give them more decisions

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.600
or do I not like the way they think

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.560
about things? Basically.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.840
Um and the second thing is

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:33.519
um they get practice. They start to

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.959
build the muscle. They start to think

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:37.040
for themselves

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:39.320
and it's just like

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.519
enabling a kid by solving every problem

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.000
for them, they're going to keep coming

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.800
to you to solve their problems, but

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.800
eventually, if they know that hey, if if

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.040
I go to Nick, he's just going to ask me

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.720
a bunch of questions. He's not going to

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:51.239
help. Um I'm I'm kind of forced to do

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.480
this myself, which

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:54.640
over time, it's how you enable, you

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.960
know, people to perform really well in

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.080
the job.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.880
>> Yeah, and ideally they just get the kind

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.280
of questions that you ask and they ask

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.560
them themselves.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.760
And they come to your office less and

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.280
less and they build the muscles.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.520
>> Yeah, and if they come to me three days

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.600
in a row with the same question three

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.480
times, that third conversation is not

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.480
going to go well for them.

